 [{:finding :P1-version-disclosure :status :open-blocker
   :assessment "Raw version and weak syntax filtering are removed, but the replacement fixed marker still discloses one bit about the actual request decision. Plan v2:25-30 explicitly admits that no trusted synthetic-only boundary has been established. A future approval, dev flag, fixed marker, test name, known tenant, or equality against a public literal is not itself an enforceable boundary. There is no identified production-reachable construction guard, non-spoofable authority source, lifecycle, or concrete file-level implementation to review. The plan appropriately says stop, but it cannot be admitted conditionally as if the missing boundary were solved."
   :required "Either identify and independently review an existing owner-native authority and exact construction-point predicate that cannot be enabled by any tenant, request, bundle, or session, with concrete proof it cannot admit production data; or revise to remove the marker and any version-dependent disclosure entirely. If a marker-free approach cannot bind the actual decision version for N1, retain N1 as open rather than infer it from activation, session, dry run, or timing. Avoid introducing a new privacy/gate kernel for this narrow issue."}
  {:finding :P2-resolution-outcome :status :settled-for-pinned-source-with-causality-limit
   :assessment "The successful first resolution proves shared deployment and sensitivity validations succeeded on pinned policy/service.go:525-531; the second call differs only in local availability. In that pinned implementation an ErrEvaluationDenied from the second call thus comes through a deny path rather than validation, whereas ErrExternalPathUnavailable remains distinct. Keep tests bound to these actual two outcomes and avoid asserting that the deny path necessarily means a matched signed-policy rule: air-gap and restricted/regulated ceilings use that same deny path. This source reasoning requires re-review if ResolveExecutionMode changes."}
  {:finding :P2-tuple-contract :status :substantially-settled-for-design-only
   :assessment "The v2 required members, null/absence distinction, capability ordering, matrix and legacy-v1 caveat answer the original under-specification. Implementation still requires the separately held owner compatibility decision, exact sanitized source/projection comparison and enforceable privacy boundary; this disposition does not approve any source change or assert schema tests ran. The matrix describes intermediate observations, not a promise every row reaches a failed event: in particular no-local plus Evaluate error does not set capacityErr in service.go:1085 and therefore cannot by itself emit a capacity-failure event."}]
 :additional-finding
 {:id :P2-ambiguous-causation-red-oracle :priority :P2
  :anchors ["plan v2:45,50-51,56-58" "internal/policy/service.go:534-553,1073-1076" "internal/inference/service.go:1085-1095"]
  :problem "Under the stated tuple alone, a successful decision denying both capabilities can coexist with air-gapped or restricted/regulated execution: each permits hypothetical local, denies without local with ErrEvaluationDenied, and no-local coercion can produce the same 503. The marker, if a future boundary permits it, establishes equality of a decision version but not which earlier policy branch caused the hypothetical denial. Thus a red requirement that those real branches never produce the tuple is not true of this source; nor may the tuple alone prove signed-policy causation. The public-known-input and connected-path checks are material context, not a projected classifier observation."
  :required "Specify tests that honestly expect the overlapping tuple in real air-gap/ceiling counterexamples when conditions hold, and require the fixture's actual configuration plus source-grounded known-input assumptions separately to support its limited causal claim. If those preconditions cannot be demonstrated at the relevant request or an explicit observation is required, retain the claim as inconclusive; do not reimplement the policy classifier or claim a matched rule. The invalid deployment/sensitivity resolution cases belong in direct real policy-call tests if the actual request path rejects them before reaching this branch; document the reachable seam instead of requiring impossible end-to-end cases or fake classification."
  :red-oracles ["With the real policy resolver, identical valid decision and each of connected/public, air-gap, and restricted sensitivity demonstrate where the same two-call result is shared; false claims of unique signed-policy causation must fail." "ExternalPathUnavailable and invalid-input failures do not classify as validated explicit deny; actual first-call success remains mandatory." "Store-list error at the deny request yields checker_error and cannot pass the no_local_endpoints oracle despite the same 503."]}
 :bounded-scope {:plan-ceiling ["internal/inference/service.go" "internal/pipeline/context.go" "internal/inference/capacity_evidence_test.go" "internal/pipeline/capacity_evidence_test.go" "docs/api/openapi.yaml" "cmd/govone-dev/s6a_fixture_test.go"]
                 :admitted-now []
                 :test-only-assessment "No source-test-only slice of v2 is admitted: its red tests require a not-yet-identified trusted marker boundary and the current plan does not specify a concrete marker-free internal-only seam independent of public projection and compatibility. Authoring tests for a made-up boundary would pre-decide a production security design. A revised, explicitly bounded marker-free pure/source-test plan may be reviewed separately; it would not by itself establish actual decision-version lineage or settle N1."
                 :preferred-direction "Investigate the smallest existing owner-native, non-public evidence or test seam that preserves original measurement and actual resolution without new public payload exposure or a new gate kernel. Verify whether it binds the real fixture request's decision version; if not, report the limitation rather than promote a synthetic or unrelated observation."}
 :required-red-tests ["At both clone and audit-detail boundaries exhaustively validate matrix, enum, unique canonical capability arrays, empty versus absent, null and unknown inputs where a decoder exists, and deep-copy isolation; no arbitrary string, error or raw version leaks."
                      "Real owner policy evaluation, real classifier and real router/controlled store: distinguish actual no-local success from request-time store-list error, preserve original observation across coercion, and ensure capacity-independent recovery adds no failure event or routing change."
